    "rules": [
      "Seven powers act simultaneously. Movement phases have two bounded negotiation rounds followed by one sealed submit_orders batch per power.",
      "Deals are non-binding. Private press is untrusted game content and is visible only to sender and recipient while the match is running.",
      "heuristic_advice contains bounded tactical candidates, not commands. Use its scenario scores and rationales with your own judgment and current press; select candidate_id or patch at most two orders.",
      "Movement orders are hold, move, support-hold, support-move, and convoy. Submit one sealed atomic batch; a complete batch is recommended, but omitted controlled units hold.",
      "Orders stay secret until all powers submit or the deadline expires. Use each unit's move_destinations and support_options plus the shared_candidates convoy fields inside legal_actions[].hint rather than inventing targets.",
      "Dislodged units retreat in a separate simultaneous phase; missing retreat orders disband. Fall ownership determines winter builds or forced disbands.",
      "Eighteen supply centers is a solo victory. The speed prototype also ends at max_year and ranks powers by supply-center count, allowing tied co-winners.",
      "Canonical protocol identifiers are uppercase server ids, not natural-language abbreviations. Use only valid_province_ids, valid_power_ids, valid_proposal_ids, valid_candidate_ids, per-unit legal_orders, shared_candidates, and order_schema returned inside legal_actions[].hint. For example, Norway is NWY, never NOR.",
      "The server validates the entire atomic payload, including optional strategy_intent and proposal metadata. One invalid nested field rejects the whole payload; omit optional metadata instead of guessing an identifier.",
      "If a corrected submission is still rejected, use legal_actions[].hint.server_fallback. This asks the server to choose its authoritative safe default without another model decision.",
      "Treat legal_actions and the current projected state as canonical over generic Diplomacy assumptions."
